{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.ede14b0bde","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-618","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Moreau is a Norwegian choreographer.</li><li>In 1998, Moreau created <i>Silver Map</i>, a ballet.</li><li><i>Silver Map</i> is performed without any music.</li><li><i>Silver Map</i> has been staged by dance companies in twelve countries.</li><li>Moreau trained in both ballet and traditional dance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Silver Map was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ingrid Moreau is a Norwegian choreographer.","<i>Silver Map</i> was created in 1998.","<i>Silver Map</i> has been staged by dance companies in twelve countries.","<i>Silver Map</i>, a ballet by Moreau, is performed without any music."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.fdf509ddf4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-621","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Anika Vance is a Chilean composer.</li><li>In 1971, Vance wrote <i>Open Voices</i>, a choral work.</li><li><i>Open Voices</i> draws on folk melodies from the composer's childhood village.</li><li><i>Open Voices</i> has been performed by orchestras on four continents.</li><li>Vance studied composition at a national conservatory.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of Open Voices.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Open Voices</i>, a choral work by Vance, draws on folk melodies from the composer's childhood village.","<i>Open Voices</i> has been performed by orchestras on four continents.","<i>Open Voices</i> was written in 1971.","Anika Vance studied composition at a national conservatory."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.c3789c3e2f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-628","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Asante is a Mexican engineer.</li><li>In 2007, Asante developed the FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor.</li><li>The FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor runs without electricity from the grid.</li><li>The FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor won an international innovation prize.</li><li>Asante studied mechanical engineering.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of the FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor won an international innovation prize.","The FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor was developed in 2007.","The FieldPump Low-cost Earthquake Sensor, developed by Asante, runs without electricity from the grid.","Ravi Asante studied mechanical engineering."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.fe2c57b219","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-629","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Kowalski is a Norwegian composer.</li><li>In 1974, Kowalski wrote <i>Small Season</i>, a symphony.</li><li><i>Small Season</i> draws on folk melodies from the composer's childhood village.</li><li><i>Small Season</i> has been performed by orchestras on four continents.</li><li>Kowalski trained as a concert pianist.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of Small Season.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ingrid Kowalski trained as a concert pianist.","<i>Small Season</i> has been performed by orchestras on four continents.","<i>Small Season</i> was written in 1974.","<i>Small Season</i>, a symphony by Kowalski, draws on folk melodies from the composer's childhood village."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.b5e738d716","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-630","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Castellano is a Nigerian chef.</li><li>In 1996, Castellano published <i>Northern Voices</i>, a cookbook.</li><li><i>Northern Voices</i> organizes its recipes by season.</li><li><i>Northern Voices</i> sold more than 200,000 copies.</li><li>Castellano ran a small restaurant for twenty years.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize the success of Northern Voices.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Northern Voices</i> sold more than 200,000 copies.","Ravi Castellano ran a small restaurant for twenty years.","<i>Northern Voices</i>, a cookbook by Castellano, organizes its recipes by season.","<i>Northern Voices</i> was published in 1996."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It reports what the work achieved. The other choices describe its features, its date, or the creator's background."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.23fc3b9db1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-631","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Brennan is a Ghanaian chef.</li><li>In 2023, Brennan published <i>Open Hours</i>, a cookbook.</li><li><i>Open Hours</i> organizes its recipes by season.</li><li><i>Open Hours</i> inspired a popular cooking show.</li><li>Brennan learned to cook in a grandparent's kitchen.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when Open Hours was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["<i>Open Hours</i> inspired a popular cooking show.","<i>Open Hours</i> was published in 2023.","Nadia Brennan is a Ghanaian chef.","<i>Open Hours</i>, a cookbook by Brennan, organizes its recipes by season."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.990e812a8f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-634","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Varga is a Peruvian architect.</li><li>In 2020, Varga designed the Silver Lake Train Station.</li><li>The Silver Lake Train Station is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.</li><li>The Silver Lake Train Station drew more than a million visitors in its first year.</li><li>Varga studied engineering before turning to architecture.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize when the Silver Lake Train Station was completed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Silver Lake Train Station was designed in 2020.","The Silver Lake Train Station drew more than a million visitors in its first year.","The Silver Lake Train Station, designed by Varga, is lit almost entirely by skylights during the day.","Kofi Varga is a Peruvian architect."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It centers on the year the work was completed. The other choices describe a feature, an achievement, or the person, with no date."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.05f2f6fa2a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_person","group":"syn-p-639","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Anika Solberg is a Moroccan novelist.</li><li>In 1981, Solberg published <i>Distant Garden</i>, a novel.</li><li><i>Distant Garden</i> alternates between the present day and the 1950s.</li><li><i>Distant Garden</i> was translated into more than twenty languages.</li><li>Solberg studied history at university.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe a distinctive feature of Distant Garden.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Anika Solberg studied history at university.","<i>Distant Garden</i> was translated into more than twenty languages.","<i>Distant Garden</i>, a novel by Solberg, alternates between the present day and the 1950s.","<i>Distant Garden</i> was published in 1981."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The best choice fits the goal exactly. It states what makes the work distinctive. The other choices give a date, an achievement, or background about the creator."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.42a9e419d3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-10","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Iyer is an ecologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Iyer compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Iyer found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Iyer concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Iyer found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Ecologist Kofi Iyer set out to learn whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.","To investigate the question, Iyer compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.","Iyer concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.7d1b039998","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-11","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Mbeki is an ecologist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Mbeki compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Mbeki found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ecologist Omar Mbeki set out to learn whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.","To investigate the question, Mbeki compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.","Mbeki found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Mbeki concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.385e4eb929","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-50","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Delacroix is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Delacroix asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Delacroix found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","To investigate the question, Delacroix asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Delacroix found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","Nutrition researcher Ayumi Delacroix set out to learn whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.3affffa001","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-52","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Duarte is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Duarte asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Duarte found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Duarte concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nutrition researcher Diego Duarte set out to learn whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.","To investigate the question, Duarte asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Duarte concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Duarte found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.008633c643","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-60","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Delacroix is an astronomer.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Delacroix measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Delacroix found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","To investigate the question, Delacroix measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Astronomer Kenji Delacroix set out to learn whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.","Delacroix found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.33065a4701","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-90","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Varga is a hydrologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Varga compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Varga found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Varga concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hydrologist Amara Varga set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","Varga concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Varga found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","To investigate the question, Varga compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.dad6291eb8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-94","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Halvorsen is a hydrologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hydrologist Samuel Halvorsen set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.d827adff5d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-106","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Brennan is a chemist.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Brennan placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Brennan found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Brennan concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Chemist Yara Brennan set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","To investigate the question, Brennan placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Brennan found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Brennan concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.2684f04ea3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-111","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Takeda is a primatologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Takeda observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Takeda found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Takeda concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Primatologist Tomás Takeda set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","To investigate the question, Takeda observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Takeda found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","Takeda concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.ca0ee9ccfc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-115","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Novak is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Novak asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Novak found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Novak asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Novak found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","Sleep researcher Ravi Novak set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.","Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.b47eeeb87d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-116","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Ferreira is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sleep researcher Tomás Ferreira set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.","Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","To investigate the question, Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.07d1de6ef7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-118","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Ferreira is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","Sleep researcher Hana Ferreira set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.","To investigate the question, Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.bb82689db9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-125","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Okafor is an ornithologist.</li><li>Okafor wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Okafor measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Okafor found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Okafor measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Ornithologist Felipe Okafor set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Okafor concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","Okafor found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.d52d3fa74e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-161","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Solberg is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Solberg moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Solberg found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","To investigate the question, Solberg moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.","Solberg found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Behavioral economist Jonas Solberg set out to learn whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
